 sequenceDiagram
     autonumber
     participant Admin as Administrator
     participant GrantTool as polar-admin-grant<br/>(admin's local tool)
     participant CredAgentObs as Credentials Agent<br/>(observer -- low trust)
     participant Cassini as Cassini broker
     participant CredAgentCon as Credentials Agent<br/>(consumer -- high trust)
     participant CertIssuer as cert-issuer
     participant CA as CA (in-process,<br/>part of cert-issuer)

     Note over Admin,CA: One-time. A hard prerequisite for everything else --<br/>someone has to be first, with nothing else yet to vouch for them.<br/>No special carve-out from here on: this goes through the observer<br/>exactly like every other flow, using a Kubernetes credential<br/>instead of an IdP token. No grant lookup -- the Kubernetes<br/>credential itself is what authorizes this one exchange.

     Admin->>GrantTool: Run tool
     activate GrantTool
     GrantTool->>GrantTool: Generate keypair locally (via csr-utils)<br/>(private key never leaves this machine)
     GrantTool->>CredAgentObs: Send CSR + kubectl-admin-backed<br/>Kubernetes credential<br/>(correlation_id generated)
     activate CredAgentObs
     CredAgentObs->>CredAgentObs: Basic well-formedness check only --<br/>no credential validation, no trust decision
     CredAgentObs->>Cassini: Forward, tagged with correlation_id
     deactivate CredAgentObs
     activate Cassini
     Cassini->>CredAgentCon: Deliver
     deactivate Cassini
     activate CredAgentCon
 
     CredAgentCon->>CertIssuer: Forward CSR + credential<br/>(direct, internal, core-to-core --<br/>both are trusted services)
     activate CertIssuer
     CertIssuer->>CertIssuer: Validate the admin's Kubernetes<br/>credential (existing trust path,<br/>no new IdP config for admins)
     CertIssuer->>CA: Sign CSR
     activate CA
     CA-->>CertIssuer: Signed, ordinary Polar client cert<br/>(no more privileged than any agent's)
     deactivate CA
     CertIssuer-->>CredAgentCon: Signed certificate
     deactivate CertIssuer
 
     CredAgentCon->>Cassini: Reply (signed cert), tagged with<br/>the original correlation_id,<br/>including the Credentials Agent's<br/>current escrow public key
     deactivate CredAgentCon
     activate Cassini
     Cassini->>CredAgentObs: Deliver correlated reply
     deactivate Cassini
     activate CredAgentObs
     CredAgentObs->>GrantTool: Signed certificate +<br/>Credentials Agent's escrow public key
     deactivate CredAgentObs
 
     GrantTool->>GrantTool: Store cert + key locally<br/>(reused for every future grant/revoke)
     deactivate GrantTool
